        },
        "acc-1": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What it is",
            "icon": "none",
            "content": "<p>Cebeam dissolving microneedle patches sit under each eye and release concentrated actives through hundreds of painless micro-cones that dissolve overnight — reaching just below the skin barrier where creams stop. Two patches, two nights a week. Press them on before bed, peel them off in the morning. That’s the whole method.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "acc-2": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why hasn’t a cream fixed this?",
            "icon": "none",
            "content": "<p>Because of where a cream stops. The skin’s outer barrier is built to keep things out, so most of what you rub on never gets past it — and under-eye products get formulated weak on purpose, or they’d sting. The dissolving micro-cones start <strong>below</strong> that barrier and deliver the actives where they can actually work. It’s a delivery difference, not a stronger cream.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "acc-3": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Does it actually work?",
            "icon": "none",
            "content": "<p>The morning after night one the area usually looks a little flatter — that’s hydration, real and temporary. The changes that hold to bags, shadows and texture build over several weeks of consistent use, because that’s how long skin takes to turn over. Anything promising it overnight is lying to you. Two nights a week is what matters.*</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "acc-4": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Who is it for?",
            "icon": "none",
            "content": "<p>Men (and women) 45+ who keep getting told they look tired when they slept fine — whether the bags are hereditary, from screens and late calls, or simply from getting older. It works on fluid, thin skin, lost firmness and crepey texture. It won’t shift inherited fat pads that push forward — that part is structural, and only surgery moves it.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "acc-5": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What’s in the cones",
            "icon": "none",
            "content": "<p><strong>Hyaluronic Acid</strong> — holds water in the tissue; this is the immediate effect.</p><p><strong>Niacinamide</strong> — works on tone and barrier strength over weeks.</p><p><strong>Peptides &amp; Collagen</strong> — signal toward firmness; the slower, week-six work.</p><p><strong>Vitamin C &amp; Retinol</strong> — smooth fine lines and even out tired-looking texture.*</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "acc-6": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How do I use them?",
            "icon": "none",
            "content": "<p>On clean, completely dry skin, press one patch under each eye for 5–10 seconds. Leave on for at least 2 hours — overnight is best — then peel off in the morning. Takes about fifteen seconds a night, two to three nights a week. No cleanser step, no serum, nothing to layer.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "acc-7": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do the patches hurt?",
            "icon": "none",
            "content": "<p>No. This isn’t a metal roller. You feel a light prickle for a minute while the micro-cones soften, then you stop noticing. They’re far too short to reach a nerve or draw blood. Sharp pain isn’t normal — if you feel it, take the patch off.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "acc-8": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How long before I see results?",
            "icon": "none",
            "content": "<p>The next morning looks fresher — that’s mostly hydration. The changes that stick take roughly 6–8 weeks, because that’s epidermal turnover and nothing shortens it. Got something in the calendar — a reunion, a round of interviews, a wedding? Count backwards and start at least eight weeks out.*</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "acc-9": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do you offer a guarantee?",
            "icon": "none",
            "content": "<p>Yes — a 90-day money-back guarantee. If you don’t see a noticeable difference, email us for a full refund. You can have opened and used the box, and nothing goes back in the post.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "acc-10": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Shipping",
            "icon": "none",
            "content": "<p>Fast, tracked shipping across the U.S. in plain, discreet packaging. You’ll get a tracking link by email as soon as your order leaves our facility.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
