    "faq": {
      "type": "ces-faq-accordion",
      "blocks": {
        "faq-1": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long until I see results?",
            "answer": "<p>A fresher look the next morning — that’s hydration. The changes that hold to bags, shadows and lines take roughly 6–8 weeks of regular use, because that’s how long skin takes to turn over.*</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "faq-2": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does it hurt?",
            "answer": "<p>No. A light prickle for the first minute while the cones soften, then you stop noticing. They’re far too short to reach a nerve. This is not the metal roller you’re picturing.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "faq-3": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is this going to turn into a routine?",
            "answer": "<p>No. Two to three nights a week is all you need — press them on before bed, peel them off in the morning. The actives keep working between uses. No serum step, nothing to layer.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "faq-4": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are they safe for sensitive skin?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. The formula is dermatologist-tested and made for the delicate eye area. If your skin reacts easily, patch test on the inner forearm and wait 24 hours first.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "faq-5": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I apply them?",
            "answer": "<p>On clean, dry skin, press one under each eye for 5–10 seconds. Leave on at least 2 hours, or overnight, then peel off in the morning. About fifteen seconds a night.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "faq-6": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why do the patches feel dry to the touch?",
            "answer": "<p>That’s the point. The cones are crystallised, solidified actives — not a soaked serum — so there’s no liquid. The patch <strong>is</strong> the dose.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "faq-7": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "A little redness after use — is that normal?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, and it’s a good sign — it means the cones delivered the actives where they’re needed. It usually settles within 15–30 minutes.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "faq-8": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will anyone be able to tell I’m using them?",
            "answer": "<p>No. There’s no colour in it and nothing sits on your face during the day — you wear them overnight and they’re gone by morning. Nothing on the bathroom shelf that needs explaining, and packaging ships discreetly.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "faq-9": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will this work on bags I’ve had for years?",
            "answer": "<p>Often, partly — and here’s the honest answer. Fluid, thin skin and lost firmness respond well. Inherited fat pads — the kind in photos of you at twenty-five — only surgery shifts, at $3,000–$6,000 and a week off work. Most men are a mix. If you’re mostly the first kind, save your money.*</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "faq-10": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why has no doctor ever mentioned this to me?",
            "answer": "<p>Mine hadn’t either. GP and dermatology appointments are short and triaged toward medical problems — cosmetic delivery methods don’t come up unless you raise them. It’s a short appointment, not a conspiracy.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "faq-11": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Who should not use these?",
            "answer": "<p>Skip them on broken, irritated or sunburned skin, or with an active eye infection. If you’re on prescription retinoids, ask your doctor first.*</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "faq-12": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How should I store them?",
            "answer": "<p>Sealed, somewhere cool and dry, out of direct sun. Don’t refrigerate — condensation ruins the micro-cones. Once a patch is out of its pouch, use it.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "faq-13": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What if it doesn’t work for me?",
            "answer": "<p>Email us within 90 days for a full refund. You don’t need to send the box back.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        }
      },
